id: pm-th6voj
title: Bound Vitest transform-cache retention and make oversized-cache startup diagnosable
description: A focused run spent minutes pruning the local Vitest cache before reporting any tests. The directory held approximately 75 MB of directory entries while four filesystem worker threads waited on unlink or writeback. The run was stopped and the cache preserved by a same-filesystem rename before retry. Add bounded retention or actionable startup diagnostics with preservation-first recovery.
type: Chore
status: open
priority: 3
tags[3]: cache,performance,testing
created_at: "2026-11-09T07:47:55.491Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-09T08:48:41.338Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Measure transform-cache growth and startup cost on a representative long-lived checkout; Provide bounded cache lifecycle or explicit actionable diagnostics without deleting user data; Keep canonical coverage and test isolation unchanged
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: medium
expected_result: "Long-lived checkouts retain bounded cache startup cost or receive actionable preservation-first diagnostics without changing test coverage, isolation or deadlines."
